{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBSrJXtJfAVcokfKvUtk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 20 (Co 0.33 / Sb 0.67) as the best composition. It had the highest EQE of the three I measured, but that EQE is only 0.055%, so I can't tell how close it is to the true best in the library.\n\nThe library had 30 compositions along a line from about 11% to 85% Sb. I had 3 merit measurements and used all of them:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 20 | 0.669 | **0.055** |\n| 25 | 0.790 | −0.001 (about zero) |\n| 17 | 0.581 | −0.107 |\n\n- **Why index 20 first:** its composition matches CoSb₂O₆, a known crystal structure (trirutile) that can act as a photoanode under visible light, and it is the most likely active phase in this system.\n- **The other two:** I measured one composition richer in Sb and one richer in Co. Both were worse, which fits activity peaking near 1:2 Co:Sb.\n\n**Limits:**\n- **Unexplored range:** everything with less than 58% Sb (17 of the 30 candidates) is unmeasured, so I can't rule out a better composition on the Co-rich end.\n- **No XRD:** I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements, so it isn't confirmed that index 20 actually contains the trirutile phase.\n- **Negative EQE at index 17:** this suggests that sample doesn't work as a photoanode, or that the signal there is noise."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":7415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"output_tokens":495,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"495045e9-882a-42c5-b0ee-fa177121b9dd","uuid":"4d727bf9-98e1-4028-a7ac-21f1a77e3b87","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:20:26.863Z","request_id":"r